## Components


### Flask Application

The Flask application is deployed on:


devA
devB
devC



The application returns:

- Hostname
- Current time


The application is managed by systemd and started automatically.


### HAProxy

HAProxy provides HTTP load balancing.

Service:


TCP port 80



Backend servers:


devA 10.0.1.11:80
devB 10.0.1.12:80
devC 10.0.1.13:80



Algorithm:


round-robin




### HAProxy Statistics

Statistics page:


http://HAproxy-IP:8011/stats



Requirements:

- Password protected
- Refresh interval: 1 second


Password is stored in:


uipassword




### Nginx UDP Load Balancer

HAProxy cannot handle UDP traffic.

Therefore Nginx is used for SNMP load balancing.


External:


UDP 1611



Internal:


UDP 161



Backend:


devA
devB
devC




### SNMP

SNMP daemon runs on:


devA
devB
devC



Listening port:


UDP 161




## SSH Access


The environment uses Bastion host as SSH jump server.


Example:



Laptop
|
|
Bastion
|
|
devA/devB/devC



SSH configuration uses:


ProxyJump bastionET2598




## Deployment


Install Ansible:



sudo apt install ansible



Test connectivity:



ansible -i hosts all -m ping



Expected:



HAproxy SUCCESS
devA SUCCESS
devB SUCCESS
devC SUCCESS




Deploy:



ansible-playbook -i hosts site.yaml




## Verification


### Test Flask service directly



curl http://10.0.1.11
curl http://10.0.1.12
curl http://10.0.1.13




### Test HAProxy



curl http://HAproxy-IP



Multiple requests should return responses from:


devA
devB
devC




### Test HAProxy statistics


Open:



http://HAproxy-IP:8011/stats



Use username:


admin



Password:


stored in uipassword




## Ansible Files


### hosts

Defines managed machines.


### site.yaml

Main deployment playbook.


### templates/

Contains configuration templates:

- HAProxy configuration
- Nginx UDP configuration
- Flask systemd service
- SNMP configuration


### files/

Contains Flask application source code.
